 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Uses",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Intended for small-signal switching and for very high speed switching duty."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Construction and marking",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "SOD-523 plastic body; the molding compound is rated UL 94V-0 for flammability, and the part is RoHS compliant and free of halogens. Terminals are solder plated and pass the solderability test of MIL-STD-750 method 2026. A band on the body marks the cathode end, and the top carries the code 61."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Power derating",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "The 150 mW dissipation holds to 25 °C ambient and falls linearly to zero at 150 °C."
  }
